        <h1 class="profile-detail-name">Wu Zetian</h1>
        <div class="info-stats" style="margin-top:10px;">
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Period</span><span class="info-stat-val">624 CE – 705 CE</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Born</span><span class="info-stat-val">17 February 624; birthplace disputed (Wenshui, Lizhou or <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/changan">Chang'an</a>); daughter of Wu Shiyue, a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/timber">timber</a> merchant who became a senior Tang official, and Lady Yang of the Yang family</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Died</span><span class="info-stat-val">16 December 705, a few months after she was removed from power in the Shenlong Coup; buried in 706 with Emperor Gaozong at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qianling-mausoleum">Qianling Mausoleum</a></span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Who they were</span><span class="info-stat-val">Concubine of Emperor Taizong; empress consort of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emperor-gaozong-of-tang">Emperor Gaozong of Tang</a>, 655–683; empress dowager and regent, 683–690; emperor (huangdi) of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zhou-dynasty">Zhou dynasty</a>, 690–705</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Known for</span><span class="info-stat-val">The only woman to take the title huangdi; founding the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zhou-dynasty">Zhou dynasty</a> in place of the Tang; rule through informants and secret police; purges of the Tang imperial house and of officials; reform of the imperial examinations; patronage of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/buddhism">Buddhism</a></span></div>
