    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>Taken to the palace at 14 as a concubine of Emperor Taizong, Wu became the favourite of his successor Gaozong and, in 655, his empress.</li><li>After Gaozong fell ill in 660 she made the daily decisions of government, and after his death in 683 she deposed one son and ruled through another before taking the throne herself in 690.</li><li>Her rule joined secret police terror and the killing of rivals, including members of her own family, with reform of the examinations and the promotion of officials from less privileged families.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p>In 690 Wu adopted a set of modified Chinese characters and took one of them, Zhao, as her formal name. It was made of the characters for light and sky, with the implication, it appeared, that she would be like the light shining from the sky.</p></aside>
    </section>

